//! MCP Tool Annotation Guard: the PDK glue.
//!
//! Every decision is made by `guard-core`. This crate reads the request,
//! evaluates the DataWeave expressions, calls `guard-core` and applies the
//! result: forward, refuse with `Flow::Break`, or rewrite a `tools/list`
//! response.
//!
//! Request phase: method rules and call enforcement. A `tools/list`
//! request carries its ids, caller and catalog key to the response phase,
//! where the list is inspected, learned and filtered.
// Generated by `make build-asset-files`. guard-core parses and validates the full
// configuration; the glue reads only the DataWeave scripts from this struct.
#[allow(dead_code)]
#[rustfmt::skip] // written by the PDK build; formatting it would be undone on the next build
